#! category: furniture
#! shrine stone - an uncut stone with a cup-shaped hollow worn into its crown
#! The hollow has to be cut INTO the crown, not stacked on it. Sitting it above
#! the mass turned the whole thing into an urn with a lid; inset, with stone
#! showing either side of the rim, it reads as a worn hollow again.
#! Body below is stipple so the stone recedes and the cup keeps the eye, and the
#! silhouette is lopsided on purpose - a symmetrical boulder reads as masonry.
